id: pm-slack-slyv
title: Explain notification routing decisions offline
description: "Expose a bounded, credential-free explanation for a verified lifecycle event, combining eligibility, ordered routing, attention policy and durable delivery evidence."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T00:29:46.063Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T10:42:04.625Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-27T10:32:14.900Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-26T20:31:08.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Each fixture event has one complete decision path; urgent bypass names its policy; suppressed events are diagnosable in one bounded command with zero network calls.
resolution: "Deliver bounded offline Slack routing explanations with named urgent policies, complete decision paths and conservative durable delivery outcomes."
expected_result: Every fixture event has a complete decision path; urgent bypasses name policy; suppressed events can be diagnosed in one bounded command without network access.
actual_result: "Current-main routing explanation suite passes through pinned pm, covering every acceptance criterion. Inspected public validation records 232 paths, 83 urgent policies, zero network calls and unchanged tracker bytes. The independent receipt-key migration remains open."
comments[35]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T00:30:06.793Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check against the current CLI and sibling pm-ops: CLI provides item/history/status SDK primitives, not Slack routing explanations. Existing pm-slack outbox records delivery and coalescing plans account for attention; pm-ops diagnostics do not own Slack attention semantics. Add an offline read-only explanation, reusing verified SDK history and existing routing/planner logic. No import/export/sync or journal mutation is introduced. Historical routes were not snapshotted, so distinguish retained evidence from current-policy evaluation and explicit uncertainty."
  "2026-10-26T00:37:49.198Z",codex-agent,"Implemented exact-revision SDK and CLI diagnosis with verified history replay, configured status roles, retained eligibility, ordered current routing, named attention policy, and receipt outcome. Reads existing SQLite storage in one read-only snapshot; no new shared mutable state or import/export/sync/journal path. Targeted suite passes 8 tests including 500 seeded policy sequences replaying older SDK revisions with CRLF variants and SDK read-back state comparisons, 12 randomized custom registries, all transport states, foreign-record skips and competing transitions at every read SQL boundary. Core output contract coverage is 100/100/100; full unchanged release thresholds will be verified in CI."
  "2026-10-26T00:39:48.745Z",codex-agent,"Public main snapshot e23ecfe: 90 items, 746 history entries, 232 complete verified paths, 83 named urgent policies, zero network calls, maximum JSON 1287 bytes and TOON 964 bytes; public tracked data has no runtime receipts so all 232 delivery outcomes correctly remain uncertain. Fingerprint unchanged. Revert proof: forcing outcome to uncertain fails the suppressed-event test; removing urgent policy selection fails the exact-receipt/urgent test (each 1 test, 0 pass, 1 fail). Restored production source. Historical blocked-to-in-progress transitions retain the existing start identity using registry roles."
  "2026-10-26T00:42:23.920Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm linked-test execution passed all 9 targeted tests (500 seeded sequences and 12 random custom status registries). Added an after-command guard so diagnosing an existing outbox does not reopen writable storage or change permissions. Local typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Native Bun acceptance found that supplying options changes its default database create behavior; retained the original constructor for writable opens and isolated read-only options to explanation reads."
  "2026-10-26T00:43:26.556Z",codex-agent,"Native Bun compatibility requires the exact runtime option spelling (readonly for Bun, readOnly for Node). Kept writable opens byte-equivalent in behavior and selected only the runtime-native option for read-only inspection. Full release gates are delegated to the existing npm/Bun CI matrix on Node 22 and 26; no thresholds or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-26T00:48:28.896Z",codex-agent,"First CI run 40250779516 passed every behavioral test but correctly rejected 99.64 percent branch coverage (five missing legacy/storage boundaries). Added real SDK-generated legacy snapshots with missing status/priority, invalid historical priorities, empty opt-in storage and an unopenable database. Explanations now include safe priority operands and explicitly identify missing historical coalescing parameters. Repeated identical state hashes refuse with event_ambiguous instead of choosing an arbitrary occurrence. Public output maxima are now JSON 1380 bytes and TOON 1058 bytes; corpus/event counts and fingerprint are unchanged. Local health has host-only pm-github version skew; both clean CI health jobs passed. No history repair or dependency bump performed."
  "2026-10-26T00:51:18.204Z",codex-agent,"Public real-data replay exposed repeated state hashes, so the identity now accepts the SDK mutation feed version (CLI event-version) as an explicit discriminator. Ambiguous hashes without a version refuse with a remedy; versioned diagnosis reports receipt_revision_not_unique and does not attribute a legacy receipt to an arbitrary event. Current public validation passes 232 complete paths with event versions: 90 items, 746 entries, 83 urgent policies, zero network calls, unchanged bytes, maxima JSON 1415 and TOON 1094 bytes. Separate mutating receipt-key migration is tracked by pm-slack-rjb1."
  "2026-10-26T00:54:36.096Z",codex-agent,"Second CI run 40251414273 passed all 563 tests on Node 22 and 26 with 100 percent lines/functions and 99.93 percent branches. The sole missed branch was a database constructor failure before a handle exists; SQLite can open a directory handle and fail only on its first query. Added an actual unreadable-file permission boundary to exercise early open failure and safe cleanup. Final linked targeted suite passed all 11 tests; pinned pm result tracking is disabled by project policy, so exact results are recorded here and the complete release-gate evidence is in the PR CI run."
  "2026-10-26T00:58:22.643Z",codex-agent,"Additional output-boundary fuzzing found that Node SQLite throws while converting oversized integer columns before application validation can skip a foreign record. Read-only evidence now selects numeric fields as text, then validates finite safe domains before returning a result. Regressions cover positive/negative Infinity, NaN text, unsafe integers and invalid priority domains. Refactored database acquisition so cleanup always owns a successfully opened handle; early open failures remain typed refusals. Targeted read-only reader branch coverage has no zero-hit branches; native compiled Bun SDK/CLI acceptance passes."
  "2026-10-26T01:01:02.926Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding coverage note: the first targeted LCOV inspection still contained a zero-hit one-character range at the catch/finally boundary, confirmed by raw V8 ranges. I recorded that claim before the inspection completed. Cleanup now runs inside the typed storage-error boundary, so close failures are also sanitized; the final targeted LCOV inspection confirms zero missed reader branches. Six focused reader tests and compiled native Bun acceptance pass. Thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T01:06:37.470Z",codex-agent,"Verified product head 12fc36f: CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40252163114 passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22 and 26. Each of four gates passed 563 tests, zero failures, with 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all four source files at unchanged thresholds. Both native compiled Bun acceptance jobs passed with zero extra explanation HTTP sends. Clean CI tracker health and generated-output verification passed. CodeQL run 40252163189 passed. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/160 is ready for review. Public-data validation: 90 items, 746 entries, 232 complete paths, 83 urgent policies, zero network calls, unchanged fingerprint, maxima JSON 1415 and TOON 1094 bytes. Item remains unclosed and unclaimed for orchestrator verification; receipt-key migration remains open as pm-slack-rjb1."
  "2026-10-26T06:43:25.472Z",codex-agent,"Resuming PR 160 after read-only review: skipped is an operator work state and cannot prove non-delivery after an ambiguous attempt. Audit all receipt-to-outcome surfaces, persist attempt evidence under the existing writer transaction, centralize outcome reduction, preserve uncertainty through all operator resolutions, and add at least 500 real send/resolve lifecycle sequences with a recording synthetic Slack reference model. Existing source work and public-data evidence will be retained."
  "2026-10-26T07:07:00.687Z",codex-agent,"Class-level audit found only three receipt reporting surfaces: routing explanation, outbox status/drain, and coalescing preview/retained manifests plus their TOON renderers. All now use deriveSlackDeliveryOutcome; compatibility state counts remain work-state counts, with independent outcome totals. Tracker digest counters are activity, not delivery, and remain unchanged. Claims/results and operator resolutions are retained separately under the existing SQLite writer fence; late completions update only their own evidence. A monotonic claim counter makes gaps conservative. The first 500-sequence recording-Slack run passed (644 requests; 78 delivered, 150 withheld, 272 uncertain); stronger random operation mixing and final focused/CI checks follow. Any unresolved attempt dominates later labels or acknowledgments under the requested any-attempt uncertainty rule."
  "2026-10-26T07:16:19.530Z",codex-agent,"Requested behavioral revert proof: restored the skipped-to-withheld mapping only in explainSlackRouting, leaving the new attempt journal and reducer intact. Command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"accepted request with a timed-out response\" test/delivery-evidence.test.ts failed with 1 test, 0 passed, 1 failed (actual withheld, expected uncertain). Restored the exact production source; the same command passes 1/1. Pinned pm linked-test run passed 18 tests including 500 seeded lifecycles, 870 recorded HTTP requests, 79 delivered / 114 withheld / 307 uncertain. New delivery-evidence source has measured 100 percent lines/branches/functions. Existing targeted outbox/coalescing/routing/interleaving regressions passed 245/245."
  "2026-10-26T07:22:53.914Z",codex-agent,"The final class fix also treats HTTP redirects after transmission as ambiguous, matching the existing safe SDK example and the no-definite-rejection rule. Fake Slack timers are now armed only after recorded acceptance, so timeout classification is deterministic under host contention. The 500-sequence oracle explicitly covers uncertain skip/retry/abandon. Native compiled Bun acceptance passes and retains two uncertain outcomes after operator acknowledgment. All original public read-only measurements remain applicable because the public copy contains no runtime receipts."
  "2026-10-26T07:27:17.138Z",codex-agent,"Implementation is ready for CI: deriveSlackDeliveryOutcome uses complete attempt evidence and independent operator journals, with conservative incomplete-history handling. Exact event reads push the key predicate into both journals and use indexes, so unrelated receipt histories are not scanned for one explanation. Local focused checks, typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and compiled native Bun acceptance pass. Existing public-copy metrics remain unchanged; the new class validation document records the oracle, concurrency boundaries and revert proof. No dependency pin or coverage threshold changed."
  "2026-10-26T07:40:27.239Z",codex-agent,"Product head 3d205aa passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40285923492: npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26, each 615 tests passed / 0 failed, 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all five sources. CodeQL run 40285923440 passed. The CI model consistently measured 500 sequences / 870 HTTP requests / 79 delivered / 114 withheld / 307 uncertain. Public replay reverified 90 items / 746 entries / 232 paths / 83 urgent policies / zero network calls / unchanged fingerprint. Final legacy guard discounts known not-sent claims when checking the network counter, preventing a refusal record from masking an unjournaled older attempt. Its focused regression, typecheck/lint and compiled native Bun acceptance pass; final exact-head CI follows this commit."
  "2026-10-26T13:20:57.754Z",codex-agent,"Resumed PR 160 after bookkeeping re-review. Clean starting head fbbca71. Replace mutable claims/attempt-counter inference with immutable started/dispatch/terminal journal records. Read-derived open attempts and explicit confirmed-first precedence will cover retired senders, pre-request refusals, recovery and operator retry/abandon; extend real transport model and boundary interleavings, record behavioral revert proof, then rerun exact-head npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-26T13:32:49.314Z",codex-agent,"Implemented immutable attempt_started/terminal pairs plus request_dispatched markers; explicit precedence is confirmed => delivered, else unknown/open dispatched => uncertain, else withheld. Counters no longer determine proof or scheduling. Shared finally completion records late refusals/retired senders independently of ownership; dead-owner recovery distinguishes pre/post dispatch. Seed 0xc1a551f1 model: 500 sequences, 734 recorded requests, 201 delivered/159 withheld/140 uncertain, including forced retry/abandon, late refusal, replacement, exceptions and cancellation. Boundary validation passed 67 tests: exception and real process crash at all 32 persistence/transport boundaries plus fixed regression and seven-boundary read snapshot race. Behavioral revert proof restored only the old mutable increment/decrement path and its counter-gap inference: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"500 seeded|late pre-request\" test/delivery-evidence.test.ts failed 2/2 (retirement sequence 1 and fixed late-refusal case reported uncertain instead of withheld). Exact source bytes restored in finally; passing model and boundary evidence recorded above. Final targeted verification and CI pending."
  "2026-10-26T13:37:09.498Z",codex-agent,"Additional class coverage: forced sender retirement/replacement injected at every one of 28 before/after SQL step boundaries for retry and abandon: 57/57 tests pass. Old-journal read-only compatibility, pair migration, inaccessible/live-owner recovery and transient terminal/post-commit exceptions pass 2/2. Targeted focused suite passes 19/19; typecheck, test-source typecheck and docstring lint pass. Updated the read-snapshot race to commit attempt proof atomically with receipt state, passing all seven read boundaries. Existing targeted 245-test regression run had 244 passes plus this now-corrected fixture; the full exact-head release gates will certify the combined final state. Complete journal test command retained with a 600-second shared-host timeout."
  "2026-10-26T13:39:18.230Z",codex-agent,"Local health verifies tracker history/integrity but strict health reports inherited extension-host version skew (pinned host 2026.10.20, installed extension 2026.10.25) plus an advisory pre-existing provenance domain warning. No pins or append-only history were changed; fresh-install CI health is the required evidence. Native compiled Bun acceptance passes (2 HTTP deliveries, 2 operator-acknowledged uncertain proofs, no git). Full linked journal command is running; changelog generation/check and typechecks/docstring lint pass."
  "2026-10-26T13:42:43.097Z",codex-agent,"The pinned linked command npx pm test pm-slack-slyv --run --match delivery-evidence --progress passed: 144 tests, 0 failures in 146 seconds, including 500 model sequences (734 requests; 201 delivered, 159 withheld, 140 uncertain), clean-exit pair checks before recovery, 32 exception/32 crash boundaries and 28 retry/28 abandon replacement boundaries. Pushed product head 5871efef1e853941a547aaa3884c8837bf013a36. Fresh-install CI release gate queued: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40332543370 ; CodeQL queued: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40332543214 . No local full release gates were run on the saturated shared host."
  "2026-10-26T13:52:31.536Z",codex-agent,"First CI attempt 40332543370 reached clean-install health/build successfully but Node 26 rejected the transient-fault test wrapper at test-source typecheck: overloaded SQLite run.apply argument tuple was narrower under fresh installed types. Replaced Function.apply with Reflect.apply, matching the other native statement wrappers. Local typecheck, build:test, docstring lint and the affected transient terminal/post-commit test pass. The old queued matrix is superseded; no failed/canceled run counts as full-gate evidence. Requeueing unchanged-threshold full npm/Bun gates at the corrected head."
  "2026-10-26T14:18:59.168Z",codex-agent,"Verified product head 229804683b8bb88b9505dd99c7d2809ff112f396: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40334571915 passed all four full release gates (npm and Bun on Node 22 and 26), each 744 tests passed / 0 failed, 100% lines/branches/functions across all five sources at unchanged thresholds. Every gate reproduced 500 model sequences / 734 HTTP requests / 201 delivered / 159 withheld / 140 uncertain, 32 exception + 32 crash boundaries and 28 retry + 28 abandon replacement boundaries. Both native compiled Bun acceptances passed; fresh-install tracker health, generated output, audit, pack, changelog and release-policy checks passed. Exact-head CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40334572040 passed. Required revert proof remains 2/2 failing with only counter path restored, then restored implementation passing 144/144 linked tests. Releasing the claim without closing the item; only final evidence-commit CI and PR read-back remain. Known separate legacy receipt identity follow-up remains pm-slack-rjb1; no new CLI/SDK defect was found."
  "2026-10-26T19:13:32.583Z",codex-agent,"Resumed PR 160 after dispatch-proof and status-classifier review. Starting head 7fffcf9 is clean. Unify delivery facts around durable dispatch/confirmed-response evidence, never exception type; share one exported registry-role transition classifier between capture, recovery and explanation. Add fixed regressions and seeded registry/transition plus typed/untyped boundary models, prove each old path fails independently, then targeted checks and exact-head npm/Bun CI. Preserve prior finished routing and public-validation evidence."
  "2026-10-26T19:22:51.032Z",codex-agent,"Both fixed regressions pass: successful package transport followed by typed storage_unavailable preserves confirmed delivery (1 attempt), and done assigned blocked captures/explains a confirmed block receipt. Transport context now propagates across wrappers with AsyncLocalStorage; successful HTTP response appends confirmation before returning. Terminal proof no longer takes a refusal/error-type parameter: no dispatch marker => not_sent; dispatched exceptions => unknown_after_send; observed confirmation wins. The exported classifySlackTransition is called by hook adapter, authoritative recovery capture and explanation using SDK readSettings/resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry. Seeded models and full affected regressions are in progress."
  "2026-10-26T19:38:20.912Z",codex-agent,"New models pass: seed 0x0d15fac7 ran 500 typed/untyped failures over all four dispatch/response/terminal boundaries (250 delivered, 125 withheld, 125 uncertain); error codes vary independently of phase, and every clean exit closes its pair. The recording fake disables connection reuse and the oracle records actual received confirmations instead of assuming network success. Seed 0x0c1a551f ran 500 transitions through 50 SDK registries (renamed/custom roles, done-as-blocked and missing roles), explaining all 358 distinct captured receipts with seven role shapes. Audit found digest close/block/start bucketing separately interpreted status names, so it now delegates to the same classifier and SDK settings as capture/explanation; validation scripts do likewise. Existing outbox/interleaving regressions and exhaustive typed SQL fault coverage are being checked next."
  "2026-10-26T19:44:55.629Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs completed. Restoring only the prior attempt/terminal/finish functions makes node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"successful post followed\" test/delivery-evidence.test.ts fail 1/1: actual withheld versus expected delivered after recorded HTTP success. Separately restoring capture to its former literal-status adapter makes node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"done configured\" test/routing-explanation.test.ts fail 1/1: actual close versus expected block. Both source files restored byte-for-byte in finally after each proof; restored fixed cases plus the corrected executable SDK example pass 3/3. Existing outbox/coalescing/interleaving run passed 236/237; its only failure was that example still using the legacy conservative callback shape, now corrected with explicit dispatch and confirmation context. No history rewrite or dependency bump was used."
  "2026-10-26T19:48:14.750Z",codex-agent,"Current read-only public replay after shared-classifier integration passed on public main e23ecfe839fbb85c55e47a1cd325abf153593d4d: 90 items, 746 entries, 232 complete paths, 83 urgent policies, zero network calls, maximum 1415 JSON / 1094 TOON bytes, unchanged tracker fingerprint 7d705863b3bbf648d5ea326dc84dfc3c7e5e33f70760d2265a5f42c97d6ca731. The exported non-git tracker was read-only and PATH contained no git. Classifier uses SDK normalizeStatusInputWithRegistry for aliases/case variants and resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry roles; no separate close-status mapping remains in digest or validation scripts. The typed-error generator now covers all nine refusal codes across every phase (36 code/phase combinations) as well as untyped errors; final CI will run that expanded model."
  "2026-10-26T19:58:13.438Z",codex-agent,"Targeted classifier/digest/hook and lifecycle boundary run passed 140/140 tests, including all 34 untyped exception, 34 typed OutboxError and 34 actual process-crash boundaries. A further SDK alias/role-less/command-fallback unit passes. Pinned linked fixed-case command passed 3/3 via pm test --run --progress. Typecheck, test-source typecheck, docstring lint, build and native compiled Bun acceptance pass. Source audit: classifySlackTransition is used by captureSlackOutbox, explanation, detectEvent hook adapter, digest aggregation and both public validation scripts; SDK status alias normalization and registry roles are authoritative, with literals confined to its fallback. Full npm/Bun gates are next; no dependency pins or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-26T20:04:29.258Z",codex-agent,"CI 40391558970 at b0ecdbe passed all 794 tests on both Node 22 and 26, including the expanded nine-code error model (500 sequences, 250 HTTP calls, 250 delivered/125 withheld/125 uncertain), 50-registry model (500 transitions, 358 explained receipts), and all 34x3 SQL fault boundaries. The unchanged coverage gate correctly refused 99.94% branch coverage: one raw HTTP-helper inherited-confirmation branch lacked a test (index.ts:1382). Added a real HTTP/SDK wrapper regression that omits explicit context forwarding, confirms one delivery, then throws typed storage_unavailable; it passes locally with one attempt. This covers the second package HTTP entry point through the shared asynchronous proof context. No product source, dependency or threshold changed in this correction; typecheck/build:test/docstring lint pass. CodeQL 40391558921 passed; this failed coverage run is not full release-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-26T20:10:54.829Z",codex-agent,"Verified source head 6e68fefce4bff9c977f11af69de7b48a10780ceb: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40392451931 passed npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26, each 795 tests passed / 0 failed, with 100% lines/branches/functions across all five sources at unchanged thresholds. All four runs reproduced 500 error sequences, nine codes, 250 recorded HTTP calls and 250 delivered/125 withheld/125 uncertain; 50 SDK registries, 500 transitions and 358 explained receipts; and 34 untyped + 34 typed + 34 process-crash boundaries. Both native compiled Bun acceptances passed, as did fresh-install tracker health, generated output, audit, pack, changelog and release-policy checks. Exact-head CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40392451639 passed. Separate old-path reverts each fail their fixed case 1/1; exact restoration and linked runner pass. Tightening the model to assert all 36 typed code/phase combinations explicitly (already verified for the fixed seed), then recording final evidence and releasing the claim without closing. Final evidence-head CI and PR read-back remain; no implementation work remains and no new CLI/SDK defect was found. Existing separate legacy receipt identity follow-up remains pm-slack-rjb1."
  "2026-10-27T10:19:53.697Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit of current main: Acceptance mapping: suppressed-event fixture returns one complete eligibility/filter/ordered-route path; urgent exact-receipt fixtures name blocker and critical bypass policies; bounded JSON/TOON explanations make zero network calls and preserve tracker/storage bytes. Current-main tests also cover SDK status roles, repeated historical state hashes, retained receipts and read-only refusal boundaries. The merged PR retains the 232-event public-data validation, all 36 typed phase/code combinations, lifecycle crash-boundary model and final 795/795 npm/Bun CI gates. Separate durable receipt-key migration is still open in pm-slack-rjb1. Delivered by PR #160, merge commit 09d45956761b0547d955258b59d63103168c217c, merged_at 2026-10-26T20:31:08Z. Focused verification follows; full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to PR CI for this tracker-only change."
  "2026-10-27T10:32:11.713Z",codex-agent,"Verified current main with `node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/routing-explanation.test.ts` via the pinned pm linked runner: PASS. Observed test counts: tests=14, pass=14, fail=0, cancelled=0, skipped=0, todo=0. Current-main routing explanation suite passes through pinned pm, covering every acceptance criterion. Inspected public validation records 232 paths, 83 urgent policies, zero network calls and unchanged tracker bytes. The independent receipt-key migration remains open."
  "2026-10-27T10:42:04.488Z",codex-agent,"Closure validation: health retains the same legacy provenance advisory as untouched main 09d45956761b0547d955258b59d63103168c217c: provenance_value_domain_invalid:claude-code:role:single_digit:23. Existing item pm-slack-health-legacy-1027 owns this advisory. Strict health is not clean; the original history bytes remain unchanged. Default health additionally reports the existing global extension version skew. No history repair or dependency change is performed."
